Patch 3003: cellVdecDecodeAu keeps AUs that arrive while the picture queue is full (VDEC_DEFER=0 restores BUSY).

libvdec decodes on its own thread and sends AUDONE when it takes an AU, so a title that got BUSY waits for the next
AUDONE before it tries again. Here decoding is synchronous, so after a BUSY no AUDONE ever came: J-Stars' opening movie
stopped after 18 AUs, the screen stayed black and the title screen never came (the idle drain then emptied the queue).
Now up to 16 AUs are kept (the title leaves AU memory alone until its AUDONE) and decoded when GetPicture or
GetPictureExt makes room, with their AUDONE and PICOUT then; EndSeq decodes every kept AU first. BUSY only when that
list is full too. The same feature as the v0.15 port's VDEC_DEFER.

Tested (US disc, attract demo with the decoder on): before, black from 30 s to the end of the run
(bench/exp/2026-11-09_0046-movie1); after, the movie runs through to the title screen at about 140 s and the demo
fights follow (bench/exp/2026-11-09_0057-movie2, 28.95 f/s over the demo).

